From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 09 Nov 2026 23:00:00 +0000
Subject: media: cedrus: decode H.264 4:0:0 monochrome pictures

High profile allows monochrome (chroma_format_idc 0) streams, which the
driver refused. The H.264 engine takes chroma_format_idc in its SPS
register, which the driver already programs from the control, so let
4:0:0 through.

A 4:0:0 picture has no chroma samples for the hardware to reconstruct.
Fill the chroma plane of the capture buffer with the value which H.264
gives the chroma of a monochrome picture (128 for 8 bits) before
decoding, so that the NV12 output is the picture's grey image.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/staging/media/sunxi/cedrus/cedrus.c      |  4 ++--
 drivers/staging/media/sunxi/cedrus/cedrus_h264.c | 22 ++++++++++++++++++++++
 2 files changed, 24 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/staging/media/sunxi/cedrus/cedrus.c b/drivers/staging/media/sunxi/cedrus/cedrus.c
index 21f2ea4..338aaf0 100644
--- a/drivers/staging/media/sunxi/cedrus/cedrus.c
+++ b/drivers/staging/media/sunxi/cedrus/cedrus.c
@@ -60,8 +60,8 @@ static int cedrus_try_ctrl(struct v4l2_ctrl *ctrl)
 	if (ctrl->id == V4L2_CID_STATELESS_H264_SPS) {
 		const struct v4l2_ctrl_h264_sps *sps = ctrl->p_new.p_h264_sps;
 
-		if (sps->chroma_format_idc != 1)
-			/* Only 4:2:0 is supported */
+		if (sps->chroma_format_idc > 1)
+			/* Only 4:2:0 and 4:0:0 (monochrome) are supported */
 			return -EINVAL;
 		if (sps->bit_depth_luma_minus8 != sps->bit_depth_chroma_minus8)
 			/* Luma and chroma bit depth mismatch */
diff --git a/drivers/staging/media/sunxi/cedrus/cedrus_h264.c b/drivers/staging/media/sunxi/cedrus/cedrus_h264.c
index 9b75d92..a37e677 100644
--- a/drivers/staging/media/sunxi/cedrus/cedrus_h264.c
+++ b/drivers/staging/media/sunxi/cedrus/cedrus_h264.c
@@ -525,11 +525,33 @@ static void cedrus_h264_irq_disable(struct cedrus_ctx *ctx)
 		     reg & ~VE_H264_CTRL_INT_MASK);
 }
 
+/*
+ * A monochrome (4:0:0) picture has no chroma samples for the hardware to
+ * reconstruct. Output them with the value which H.264 gives the chroma of
+ * a 4:0:0 picture, 1 << (BitDepthC - 1).
+ */
+static void cedrus_h264_fill_mono_chroma(struct cedrus_ctx *ctx,
+					 struct cedrus_run *run)
+{
+	struct vb2_buffer *buf = &run->dst->vb2_buf;
+	size_t luma = (size_t)ctx->dst_fmt.bytesperline * ctx->dst_fmt.height;
+	size_t size = vb2_plane_size(buf, 0);
+	u8 *vaddr = vb2_plane_vaddr(buf, 0);
+
+	if (!vaddr || size <= luma)
+		return;
+
+	memset(vaddr + luma, 0x80, min_t(size_t, ctx->dst_fmt.sizeimage, size) - luma);
+}
+
 static int cedrus_h264_setup(struct cedrus_ctx *ctx, struct cedrus_run *run)
 {
 	struct cedrus_dev *dev = ctx->dev;
 	int ret;
 
+	if (!run->h264.sps->chroma_format_idc)
+		cedrus_h264_fill_mono_chroma(ctx, run);
+
 	cedrus_engine_enable(ctx);
 
 	cedrus_write(dev, VE_H264_SDROT_CTRL, 0);
-- 
